From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:12:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Give GDI only the dirty rectangle of a surface, start a
 discarding GetDC on nothing, and fail as Windows does.

As measured on Windows 11 build 29671:
- ReleaseDC keeps what GDI drew inside the dirty rectangle only, an empty one keeping nothing and none all of it;
- GetDC with discard hands GDI a surface of zeros, and ReleaseDC then keeps all of it;
- a second GetDC, a ReleaseDC without a DC and GetDC on a surface that is not GDI compatible fail with
  DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL, leaving the caller's handle as it was;
- a GDI compatible texture is a render target of one level (any number of layers), anything else being
  E_INVALIDARG at creation.

Device creation no longer complains about the flags every device here honours anyway: BGRA support, single
threaded use, no internal threading optimisations and no layer settings from the registry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

